{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUf6Gx95rwwAazRzZYcKs7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd099-shred\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/shred: Overwrite a File to Hide Its Contents, and Optionally Delete It\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship shred. GNU shred overwrites files with random data to make\n6\t  recovery difficult. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n7\t  (gshred, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n8\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Overwrite file contents with random data to prevent recovery.\n12\t  - G2: Support configurable overwrite iterations, final zero pass, and file removal.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gshred via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Overwrite behavior\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must overwrite each FILE with random data for 3 iterations by default, then optionally remove the file.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"-n N or --iterations=N must set the number of overwrite passes to N.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-z or --zero must add a final overwrite pass with zeros to hide the shredding.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: \"-u or --remove must truncate and remove the file after overwriting. Without -u, the file is overwritten but not deleted.\"\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Output and size control\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print progress information to stderr for each overwrite pass.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-s N or --size=N must shred only the first N bytes. N may use unit suffixes (K, M, G).\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, shredding each in order.\n37\t      - R2.4:\n38\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or overwritten, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n47\t      - R3.3:\n48\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n49\t\n50\tnon_goals:\n51\t  - cmd/shred does not guarantee unrecoverability on journaled or log-structured filesystems.\n52\t  - cmd/shred does not implement --random-source.\n53\t\n54\tacceptance_criteria:\n55\t  - id: AC1\n56\t    criterion: \"shred file overwrites the file with random data for 3 passes, matching gshred.\"\n57\t    traces:\n58\t      - R1.1\n59\t  - id: AC2\n60\t    criterion: \"shred -n 1 -z -u file overwrites once, zeros, and removes, matching gshred.\"\n61\t    traces:\n62\t      - R1.2\n63\t      - R1.3\n64\t      - R1.4\n65\t  - id: AC3\n66\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gshred passes.\"\n67\t    traces:\n68\t      - R1.1\n69\t      - R1.2\n70\t      - R1.3\n71\t  - id: AC4\n72\t    criterion: \"cmd/shred compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n73\t    traces:\n74\t      - R1.1\n75\t      - R1.2\n76\t      - R1.3\n77\t      - R1.4\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.2\n80\t      - R2.3\n81\t      - R2.4\n82\t      - R3.1\n83\t      - R3.2\n84\t      - R3.3\n85\t\n86\tpackage_contract:\n87\t  imports:\n88\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n89\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce691e4a-a1d3-4c1b-9314-e5022ba41c73","uuid":"d69c09a1-8983-4a60-9de0-c2c6bce87772","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:13:31.561Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5595/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd099-shred.yaml","content":"id: srd099-shred\ntitle: \"cmd/shred: Overwrite a File to Hide Its Contents, and Optionally Delete It\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship shred. GNU shred overwrites files with random data to make\n  recovery difficult. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gshred, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Overwrite file contents with random data to prevent recovery.\n  - G2: Support configurable overwrite iterations, final zero pass, and file removal.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gshred via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Overwrite behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must overwrite each FILE with random data for 3 iterations by default, then optionally remove the file.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-n N or --iterations=N must set the number of overwrite passes to N.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-z or --zero must add a final overwrite pass with zeros to hide the shredding.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-u or --remove must truncate and remove the file after overwriting. Without -u, the file is overwritten but not deleted.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Output and size control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print progress information to stderr for each overwrite pass.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-s N or --size=N must shred only the first N bytes. N may use unit suffixes (K, M, G).\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, shredding each in order.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or overwritten, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/shred does not guarantee unrecoverability on journaled or log-structured filesystems.\n  - cmd/shred does not implement --random-source.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"shred file overwrites the file with random data for 3 passes, matching gshred.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"shred -n 1 -z -u file overwrites once, zeros, and removes, matching gshred.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gshred passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/shred compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
